# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "I'm just using the Open Plan, but I had to put in my credit card.  Will I be charged? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-my-credit-card-will-i-be-charged}"
msgstr "Saya hanya menggunakan Open Plan, tapi saya harus memasukkan kartu kredit. Apakah saya akan ditagih? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-my-credit-card-will-i-be-charged}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You will not be charged unless you create a Pay-As-You-Go [instance](/guides/instances) and use it to send workloads to QPUs. See [Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) for instructions to set a cost limit and to learn about other ways to manage costs.\n"
msgstr "Kamu tidak akan ditagih kecuali jika kamu membuat [instance](/guides/instances) Pay-As-You-Go dan menggunakannya untuk mengirim workload ke QPU. Lihat [Kelola biaya](/guides/manage-cost) untuk instruksi menetapkan batas biaya dan untuk mengetahui cara lain mengelola biaya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What's the difference between an API key and an API token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"
msgstr "Apa perbedaan antara API key dan API token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There's no difference.  The terms API key and API token are used interchangeably. You'll see both terms in the documentation because different interfaces use different terms.\n"
msgstr "Tidak ada perbedaan. Istilah API key dan API token digunakan secara bergantian. Kamu akan melihat kedua istilah dalam dokumentasi karena antarmuka yang berbeda menggunakan istilah yang berbeda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What's the difference between an API token and a bearer token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr "Apa perbedaan antara API token dan bearer token? {#whats-the-difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An API token is a long-lived credential used to [authenticate to IBM Quantum Compute Service](/guides/hello-world#install-and-authenticate).  A bearer token is a temporary credential that is used to [authenticate to the REST API in an untrusted environment](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-to-the-rest-api-in-an-untrusted-environment).  A bearer token cannot be used to authenticate to IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "API token adalah kredensial yang bertahan lama yang digunakan untuk [mengautentikasi ke IBM Quantum Compute Service](/guides/hello-world#install-and-authenticate). Bearer token adalah kredensial sementara yang digunakan untuk [mengautentikasi ke REST API di lingkungan yang tidak dipercaya](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-to-the-rest-api-in-an-untrusted-environment). Bearer token tidak bisa digunakan untuk mengautentikasi ke IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do I have to choose the region that I live in? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-region-that-i-live-in}"
msgstr "Apakah saya harus memilih region tempat saya tinggal? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-region-that-i-live-in}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "No. You can use either region.  The region determines where jobs are run and where the data is kept.  Additionally, you can only see and use instances that were created in the instance that you are logged in to. Note that only the us-east region supports the Open Plan.\n"
msgstr "Tidak. Kamu bisa menggunakan region mana pun. Region menentukan di mana job dijalankan dan di mana data disimpan. Selain itu, kamu hanya bisa melihat dan menggunakan instance yang dibuat di instance yang kamu masuki. Perlu diperhatikan bahwa hanya region us-east yang mendukung Open Plan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can I connect through a proxy server? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-server}"
msgstr "Bisakah saya terhubung melalui proxy server? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-server}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, but you must use `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.44.0 or later.\n"
msgstr "Bisa, tapi kamu harus menggunakan `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.44.0 atau yang lebih baru.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is the data retention policy? {#what-is-the-data-retention-policy}"
msgstr "Apa kebijakan retensi data? {#what-is-the-data-retention-policy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM retains your (undeleted) job and usage data for three years while you continue to use IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "IBM menyimpan data job dan penggunaan kamu (yang tidak dihapus) selama tiga tahun selama kamu terus menggunakan IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What happened to Python distributions such as Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Nature, and Qiskit Experiments? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-as-qiskit-aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"
msgstr "Apa yang terjadi pada distribusi Python seperti Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Nature, dan Qiskit Experiments? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-as-qiskit-aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, the command `pip install qiskit` will **only** install the [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). This means that some modules that you have used in the past, such as `qiskit-aer` or `qiskit-nature`, now have to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr "Sejak rilis Qiskit SDK v1.0, perintah `pip install qiskit` **hanya** akan menginstal [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). Ini berarti beberapa modul yang pernah kamu gunakan sebelumnya, seperti `qiskit-aer` atau `qiskit-nature`, sekarang harus diinstal secara terpisah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit was comprised of many different Python distributions, such as `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum rilis Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit terdiri dari banyak distribusi Python yang berbeda, seperti `qiskit-terra`, inti compiler; `qiskit-aer`, simulator berperforma tinggi; provider IBM Quantum&reg; asli; dan beberapa paket yang kini sudah usang yang menyediakan fitur algoritmik eksploratif atau eksekusi eksperimen tertentu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These separate software packages were combined into what was called the Qiskit *metapackage*, which allowed users to install all of these components together through `pip install qiskit`. This metapackage architecture was removed with the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, and now each of the individual software distributions needs to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr "Paket-paket perangkat lunak terpisah ini digabungkan menjadi apa yang disebut Qiskit *metapackage*, yang memungkinkan pengguna menginstal semua komponen ini sekaligus melalui `pip install qiskit`. Arsitektur metapackage ini dihapus dengan rilis Qiskit SDK v1.0, dan sekarang setiap distribusi perangkat lunak individual perlu diinstal secara terpisah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want to install the packages that were previously included in the Qiskit metapackage, visit the [Qiskit ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) to find a range of packages to suit your needs. You can also read the [v1.0 migration guide](/guides/metapackage-migration) for more information about this change.\n"
msgstr "Jika kamu ingin menginstal paket yang sebelumnya termasuk dalam Qiskit metapackage, kunjungi [ekosistem Qiskit](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) untuk menemukan berbagai paket yang sesuai dengan kebutuhanmu. Kamu juga bisa membaca [panduan migrasi v1.0](/guides/metapackage-migration) untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang perubahan ini.\n"

